# The files every machine touches.
#
# Developer-Guide.md says these six need a word in
# #staff-updates before they are edited, because a change in any of them lands on
# everybody else's work without warning. Until now that rule was prose with nothing
# behind it: nothing asked, nothing checked, and it was forgotten as often as
# it was kept.
#
# A leading slash pins the pattern to the repository root, the same way a
# gitignore pattern works. Without it, launcher/app/Shell.cs would also match any
# Shell.cs in any folder added later.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO. GitHub requests a review from the owner named
# here when a pull request touches the file, and never asks a pull request's
# own author. So a pull request one of the team opens on Shell.cs asks the
# others, which is exactly the intent. The owners are the handles on the six
# shared files below. The guide does not keep a separate list of people.
# tests\test-branch-rules.js checks every other line stays inside that set.
#
# It is a request and nothing more. Branch protection on main, since 25
# September: enforce_admins is off; there is no required check; required
# approving reviews is 0; and Require review from Code Owners is off. The
# team's rule is to merge once the build check on the VPS is green and it
# has been said in #staff-updates, whether or not anybody named here has
# read it.
#
# Switching the code owner review on is Patrick's decision, and it is not
# free. With enforce_admins back on, a pull request of his that touches /.github/
# could never merge, because he is its only owner and GitHub does not let an
# author approve their own. Every one of his that touches the shared files
# below would wait for somebody else. The settings change without a commit, so read
# them rather than this comment:
#
#     gh api repos/EvilPatrick06/Thornswood/branches/main/protection
#
# A mistyped path or a handle without push access is ignored in silence, which
# is why the check is worth running after any edit here:
#
#     gh api repos/EvilPatrick06/Thornswood/codeowners/errors

/launcher/app/Shell.cs        @EvilPatrick06 @WiccanDjinn @Jhinswife
/launcher/app/Checks.cs       @EvilPatrick06 @WiccanDjinn @Jhinswife
/launcher/app/Keep.cs         @EvilPatrick06 @WiccanDjinn @Jhinswife
/launcher/app/Hold.cs         @EvilPatrick06 @WiccanDjinn @Jhinswife
/launcher/app/Updater.cs      @EvilPatrick06 @WiccanDjinn @Jhinswife
